      "claim": "Water has a significantly higher specific heat capacity than land materials (soil/rock).",
      "evidence": "Physics principle: Specific heat of water is approx 4.18 J/g°C, while dry soil is approx 0.8 J/g°C.",
      "weight": 0.2,
